notes.content:
A small patch with some bugfixes and adjustments to things introduced in the latest patch, along with some changes to combat feedback and animations.

Changelog

New Features:

 Added new attack animations for pets;
 Added new attack animations for specific weapons;


Adjustments:

 Improved critical hit feedback;
 Added shortcuts to "Gem Melding", "Gem Alchemy" and "Gem Storage" menus between them;
 Improved the Pet's hidden element information display on the "Pets" menu;
 Pet's hidden element is now also shown as an icon on your Pet list while having the "Rune of the Beastmaster" equipped;
 Improved Pet sorting on the Pets menu;


Balancing Adjustments:

 Reduced the stats of the following Badges:
 - Scholar;
 - Know-It-All;
 Increased the number of stacks of bleed applied by pets while using the "Rune of the Beastmaster";


Bugfixes:

 Fixed bread not healing HP when Rune of Magic Absorption was equipped;
 Fixed some attack particle effects not rendering correctly;
 Beard type name no longer displays incorrectly if you're wearing a helmet during character creation;
 "Panacea" spell no longer removes player buffs;
 Fixed "Mini-Mushroom" Pet element and stats not working correctly;

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Changed the background of the "Card Flipper" minigame;
 Added a description on how to unlock each "Card Flipper" challenger;
 Added a golden border effect to special rare cards;
 Improved sorting of the "Weapons" category in the Loot Buyer shop;
 Improved sorting of Weapons and Shields in the Equipment menu;


Balancing Adjustments:

 Adjusted the stats of the following enemies:
 - Frostdrake
 - Cave Dragon
 - Decayed Drake
 - Decayed Wyvern
 Adjusted the stats of the following items:
 - Demonblood Blade
 - Strike Amulet
 - Armor of Thorns
 - Crown of Thorns
 - Legendary Sword (Crest);
 Improved the enemy AI in the "Card Flipper" minigame;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed Items not sorting properly on the Equipments menu

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Added an animation to portals;


Balancing Adjustments:

 Increased the quantity of Soul Shards dropped by every boss;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed the "Sharpen" spell displaying incorrect values;
 Fixed some texts not fitting properly inside the description boxes;
 Fixed some text misalignment issues;
 Fixed a requirement missing from "The Golden Spoon" quest;

Changelog

Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug that caused the game to spawn an enemy from the wrong dungeon;

A very tiny patch, just to address a couple of bugs.

Changelog

Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug preventing you from increasing your sold quantity to higher than 99 using the single "+" button;
 Fixed a bug where the game wouldn't remember your fullscreen setting correctly, causing it to flicker on launch;

A very small patch, but with a feature that I've been working on for the last few days: the World Map. This will replace the Dungeon Selection list, as a more visual and interesting way to select a dungeon, while also serving as a way to give players a sense of place and scale of the world of Dungeon Mori. I hope you all enjoy this new addition!

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Changed the "Dungeon Selection" screen to a World Map;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug that caused some progression quests regarding the Spell Shop to be missing;

With this patch comes some new, much needed fixes, along with a few QoL adjustments to interfaces. Now it should be a bit easier to pick and choose between weapon options for melee classes. 

Note: If you have any of the adjusted items equipped to your character, it is recommended that you unequip it and save the game before updating to avoid any bugs that might occur.

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Added some missing stats to the "Pet Equipment" interface;
 Added missing stats to the "Equipment" interface;
 Added missing stats to the "Exploration Info" interface;
 Added a "Total Attack" stat display;



Balancing Adjustments:

 Reduced the Attack Speed bonus of the "White Swallow's Ring" accessory;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug that caused reallocating stats while having a Badge equipped would glitch the stats and subtract its value from the player;
 Fixed a bug that caused reallocating stats while having a Pet equipped with gems would glitch the stats and subtract their value from the player;
 Fixed a bug that caused level scaling effects to increase to values much higher than intended on certain difficulty settings;
 Fixed some spacing typos;
 Fixed some more quests not showing up on legacy save files imported from the demo;

Just a minor update. A few more bugs fixed, a few more items added.

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Added a new spell: Blood Spear;
 Added new accessories: 
 - Stone Dragon Talisman;
 - Wooden Wolf Talisman;
 Equipped gems will now show their name on the "Slot" text;



Balancing Adjustments:

 Increased the scaling of some late game spells;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug that caused pet damage to scale incorrectly with difficulty;
 Fixed a bug when using the "Vampiric Orb" spell that caused the game to crash;
 Fixed a few bugs regarding legacy save importing;

Another small patch with some QoL changes and a couple of new items.

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Enemies now won't run away from combat on the "Assisted" and "Average" difficulties;
 Added new accessories:
 -Wooden Skull Talisman;
 -Evil Eye Pendant;
 Dodge chance now displays the effective limit when hovering the stat icon;


Balancing Adjustments:

 Lowered the quantity of rare items required to progress certain quests;
 Lowered the quantity of boss items to 1 for dungeon unlock quests;
 Lowered the maximum effectiveness of high dodge chance against enemies;

Due to player feedback, this patch balances a lot of enemy drop rates in order to favor less grinding and incentivize a bit more variety and experimentation. It also makes a bit more comfortable for players who want to start another character.

Changelog

Adjustments:
 New accessories added to the shop:
 - Precise Arms Amulet;
 - Precise Sword Amulet;
 - Precise Staff Amulet;
 - Wooden Thorned Ring;
 - Unlucky Star Pendant;
 - Rusty Skeleton Key;
 Your Lockpicking bonus is now displayed when hovering the Lockpicking icon;
 Changed the icon of the "Rare Coin" and "Precious Coin" items;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Greatly increased the drop rate of many rare items and items required for Quests;
 Reduced the requirements for the "Monster Hunter", "Monster Slayer" and "Monster Bane" Badges and Achievements;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed a bug that showed only the last two digits of status effects if it went above 99;
 Fixed a legacy save compatibility issue with the Bestiary related quests;
 Fixed a legacy save compatibility issue with the Special Shipment questline;
 Fixed a few minor bugs;

With this update comes some adjustments to Soul Gems and pets.

Now the first effect of a Soul Gem is tied to their type, along with some effect rate adjustments and some new effects added to the pool. Do note that these changes will only take effect on new saves (created in v1.2.0 forward), as they would break earlier saves. Older saves will still remain with the previous Soul Gem system.

Pets also had their slots rebalanced, but if you have gems incompatible with the new slots, don't worry, you won't lose them. The slot will update automatically when you remove the equipped gem.

Now Soul Gems are divided into the following types:

Radial (Fighter): 
Includes effects that directly boost your physical attack power and/or favors the fighter playstyle;
Moon (Mage):
Includes effects that boost your magic attack power, spells, mana and favors the mage playstyle;
Triangle (Thief):
Includes effects that boost your critical, dodge and lockpicking, favoring the thief playstyle;
Circle (Defensive)
Includes effects that increases your HP, regeneration and defenses, supporting any playstyle defensively.

With these changes, there will be a bit more strategy involved with your pet selection, along with more thematic cohesion. With all that said, here's the changelog for this version:

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Reworked the Soul Gem system;
 Stats shown when equipping Soul Gems to pets are now the same as the stats shown when changing equipments;
 Added an option to toggle a confirmation prompt when running from combat;
 Added a button to sell all of your selected item to the "Junk Buyer" shop;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Changed all pet Soul Gem slots to better fit their niche and theme;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed equipped Soul Gems on the "Equip Pet" interface not showing their values properly;
 Fixed crashes from old saves imported from the Demo;

Do note that, while I appreciate all the feedback, I'll start working on adding the next dungeon soon, so bugfixes and small quality of life features will be prioritized in place of major game changing updates. Some suggestions might be considered for future dungeons or features, so even if I don't implement everything suggested, it is always appreciated.

Thank you for your support and understanding!

A few more quality of life adjustments along with some needed bugfixes. Thank you for the community members which reported these.

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Added a small tutorial on the first time you collect a Badge;
 Added a preview when hovering an equipped gem on the "Pets" screen;
 Changed the difficulty default to hardcore, along with a change to the preview indicating it's the intended difficulty for the game;
 Changed the "Normal" difficulty name to "Average", to better indicate it's intention;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Increased the drop rate of the "Crown and Armor of Thorns" items;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed the "Dark Furball" pet appearing as a slime when equipped to a female elf;
 Fixed the "Black Tunic" item having HP regeneration;
 Fixed the Equipped gem description showing duplicated text;
 Fixed some quests not showing up properly on older saves imported from the Demo;
 Fixed a bug that caused the Agility stat to revert incorrectly on specific levels;

With this new update, I'm bringing some suggested quality of life changes, especially to the Bestiary, along with some new accessories added to the shop.

I also want to thank the support of all the players, your feedback and comments help me to make the game better, and I hope to keep making it even better with your continued support.

And now, without further ado, here are the changes.

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Close enemy names will be shown on the dungeon when wielding a torch or any other item that emits light;
 Enemies now have each a set difficult of running past them;
 Enemies in bestiary will show their loot after only killing the quantity set in the midpoint instead of the full bar;
 Enemies in bestiary will show their exact drop rates only after killing the full amount required;
 Enemies in bestiary will now show the depth of the dungeons in which they appear;
 "Slimed Skeleton" no longer appears in the Forsaken Graveyard dungeon;
 Added the following Accessories:
Life Ring +1/+2;
Mana Ring +1/+2;
Friendship Talisman;
Goblin Amulet /+1/+2;
Ring of Divine Favor /+1/+2;
Lone Wolf Necklace
Grug's Neckalce
Cursed Skull Talisman

Balancing Adjustments:
 Increased the Drop Rate bonus of the "Avid Collector" badge;
 Increased the Defense of the Royal Knight Helm;

Bugfixes:
 Adjusted a misaligned pixel of the General Store button, on the Village screen;
 Fixed consumables not showing the correct quantity on storage while on the shop menu;
 Fixed a crash that would happen when playing Card Flipper against certain opponents on an older imported save;
 Fixed certain bestiary entries not present on an older imported save;
 Fixed some typos on certain items' descriptions;

New update to the demo, adding a few minor quality of life changes and improvements, along with some minor bugfixes.

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Added a difficulty option - can be altered at any time and changes how much the player damage scales with level;
 Added an icon to the Bestiary list to more easily indicate when you completed an entry;
 Added a proper icon showing the shortcut key to the hovering menu when highlight a field on the town menu;
 Changed the icon of the "Rusting Powder" item;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Increased the effectiveness and duration of the "Enchant Weapon" skill;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed the "Fire Enchantment" spell scaling incorrectly;
 Fixed the battle text displaying incorrectly for some status effects;
 Fixed the damage text on pet attacks not showing the color correctly;
 Fixed the battle text on "Toxic Fog" displaying incorrectly;
 Fixed "Silver Winged Circlet" item not showing when equipped on male felines;
 Fixed a bug where the game would lower the combat speed when loading a save file;

Just a small patch to address some minor issues.

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Added "Cool Drink" to the General Store;
 Added "Energy Drink" to the General Store;
 Reworked the sprite of the "Antidote" item;
 Reworked the way stats are shown on the small status screen;
 Revised the texts shown on the Mage's Guild, Loadout, Inn and Adventurers Guild interfaces;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Reduced the price of the "Antidote" item;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed the pet not leveling up displaying incorrectly;
 Fixed an issue when using the "Sharpen" spell;
 Fixed the Exp displaying incorrectly when at the max level for the demo;
 Fixed you being able to obtain exp from quests even while being at the max level for the demo;
 Fixed new items in the general store not displaying on old saves;

I've made a few adjustments based on player feedback, I hope these serve to improve your experience. While this patch also includes a few bugfixes, some of the technical issues are still being investigated. I hope the balances and additions serve to make your experience more fun, so without further ado, here are the patch notes:

Changelog

Adjustments:
 Added a small numeric display showing the recovered value when you use a consumable while exploring the dungeon;
 Added a small pointer to the bestiary indicating when you unlock partial information about the enemy;
 Improved the 'Rest' interface by showing your current HP and MP on it;
 Changed the colored area of the Feline's eyes;
 Added a mouseover display showing the item description on the 'Consumables' menu;
 Added a mouseover display showing the description of the equipped weapon skill;
 Now when your health is below 25%, the numbers will be colored red (while exploring the dungeon);
 Changed the location of the "Junk Buyer" store to the Town menu;
 Added a small dialogue after you complete the "Slime Dungeon", to show that you've finished the Demo's content;
 Changed the level cap of the Demo from 99 to 15;
 You can now pin up to 3 quests to track their progress while you explore the Dungeons;
 Added a new tab to the Dungeon Exploration side menu, showing your pinned Quests;
 Added a description when you hover your chosen "Gift" icon on the Character Creation;
 Added a new cursor option to the "Options" screen;

Balancing Adjustments:
 Rebalanced the "Guard" Skill to be more effective earlier in the game;
 Rebalanced the "Power Guard" Skill;
 Increased the effectiveness of the "Peasant Uprising" Skill;
 Rebalanced the "Primal Scream" Skill;
 Increased the duration of the "Sword's Dance" Skill;
 Increased the effectiveness of the "Battle Cry" Spell;
 Adjusted the scaling of the "Fire Weapon" Spell and increased it's duration;
 Adjusted the scaling of the "Iron Will" Spell;
 Decreased the effectiveness of the "Magic Shield" Spell and increased it's duration;
 Decreased the effectiveness of the "Smoke Screen" Spell and increased it's duration;
 Increased the duration of the "Stone Skin" Spell;
 Decreased the effectiveness of the "Strong Magic Shield" Spell;
 Increased the duration of the "Accursed Skull" item effect;
 Increased the duration of the "Dung Ball" item effect;
 Decreased the price and increased the duration and damage of the "Lacerating Knife" item effect;
 Decreased the price and increased the duration and damage of the "Poisoned Knife" item effect;
 Decreased the price and increased the damage of the "Throwing Knife" item;
 Increased the duration of the "Rusting Powder" item effect;
 Increased the duration of the "Voodoo Doll" item effect;
 Small Stones now have a small chance to stun enemies on hit;

Bugfixes:
 Fixed a small visual bug when highlighting certain fields during character creation;
 Fixed a bug that caused stats to change incorrectly when refreshing an already applied buff or debuff;
 Fixed a bug showing that the pet didn't level up even when it did in the "Rewards" screen;
 Fixed playtime still showing up when deleting a save file;

Another small update adding a few requested features plus some bugfixes.

Changelog

Adjustments:

 Added dialogue to boss fights (when entering fights and defeating bosses);
 Added a way to compare shop items to equipped items while inside the shops;
 Added an icon that shows up when the game autosaves;
 Increased the number of bleed stacks that bleed based skills inflict;
 Added a small tutorial after character creation;
 Added a new NPC to the Inn: Yulia, the Innkeeper;
 Removed the "skip intro" prompt, added a skip button to the intro in place;
 Changed the skill of the "Purple Heater Shield" to "Shield Bash";
 Added a new item to the General Store: Milk;


Bugfixes:

 Fixed a bug that caused certain buffs to last a turn longer than intended;
 Fixed a bug causing the name randomizer to not work;
 Fixed the Caps Lock button not working on the Pet Rename interface;
 Fixed some items displaying the incorrect value when using them during battle;
 Fixed a bug when canceling interface after purchasing a spell;

Update v0.1.2 is here with a small list of important bugfixes and adjustments that will carry over to the final game. Here's the list of changes:

Changelog

Adjustments:

You can now name your pets!
Added keyboard shortcuts to the Town Map screen;
Name can now be inputed directly via keyboard on the name select screen;
Added randomize buttons to character creation;
Reworked the "Channel Spells" interface;
Reworked the "Magic" and "Skill" interfaces when in combat;


Bugfixes:

Fixed a crash when cancelling out of the confirmation screen on the "Reallocate Stats" menu;
Fixed a bug that happened when trying to replace a status ailment with one of the same kind on the enemy;
Fixed a bug causing stats to decrease when leveling up on specific conditions;


I hope you've been enjoying the demo so far, and remember that player feedback is always welcome!
